{"adoption_status":"unknown","artifact_refs":[],"attrs":{},"entry_id":"9a76ba60b37766f6fa2dbecdab72ad4c","epistemic_status":"asserted","evidence_ids":["ad653a34e331f0fe0c8dbd6d9f0d1679","e012ce2a81c5ba05a2831f2de3dea0c5"],"kind":"conclusion","observed_at_seq":53,"producer":"deterministic-prototype-v0.1","record_id":"9a76ba60b37766f6fa2dbecdab72ad4c","revision":1,"run_id":"openhands-Anthropic__Claude-Sonnet-4-20250514-Thinking-setup-custom-dev-env-db035eef","source_step_ids":[53],"text":"I have successfully set up your Linux machine with zsh, oh-my-zsh, and miniconda as requested. Here's what was accomplished:\n\n## Zsh and Oh-My-Zsh Setup:\n✅ Installed zsh\n✅ Installed oh-my-zsh \n✅ Configured the \"apple\" theme\n✅ Installed and configured the requested plugins:\n   - git (default)\n   - z (for directory jumping)\n   - zsh-autosuggestions (for command suggestions)\n   - zsh-syntax-highlighting (for syntax highlighting)\n✅ Set zsh as the default shell\n✅ Configuration saved to `/root/.zshrc`\n\n## Miniconda Setup:\n✅ Downloaded and installed Miniconda3 (py39_4.12.0) \n✅ Initialized conda for both bash and zsh shells\n✅ Created `terminal-bench` environment with Python 3.10\n✅ Configured auto-activation of `terminal-bench` environment on login for both shells\n\n## Cross-shell Compatibility:\n✅ Conda works in both zsh and bash without extra configuration\n✅ The `terminal-bench` environment activates automatically in both shells\n✅ Both `/root/.zshrc` and `/root/.bashrc` are properly configured\n\nThe setup is complete and ready to use. When you start a new shell session (either zsh or bash), the `terminal-bench` conda environment will automatically activate with Python 3.10 available. The zsh session will have the apple theme and all requested plugins active."}
